WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.747
"Sleep and Anti-Aging Properties
of Melatonin Supplements"

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.000
Some experts recommend melatonin

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.840
as a first-line agent
to treat insomnia

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.400
in older adults.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.640
The World Sleep Society
disagrees

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.720
due to its low efficacy.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.320
Subjectively,
people report better sleep,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.720
though objectively,
a meta-analysis of studies

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.720
found that melatonin
only helped people

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.000
get to sleep 4 minutes faster

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
and extend
overall sleep duration

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
by about 13 minutes.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.600
If you do want to try melatonin
to help with sleep,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.800
older adults are advised

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.160
to use the smallest
effective dose

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.840
an hour before bedtime,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:42.080
starting perhaps
at 0.3 milligrams.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.440
The 12-milligram supplements
on the market

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.840
could produce levels
in the bloodstream

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.520
that can be
two hundred times higher

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:52.240
than normal nightly levels,
which raises safety concerns.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.200
After all,
melatonin used to be known

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.800
as the anti-gonad hormone,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.360
with human-equivalent doses
of just a milligram or two

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.240
reducing the size of sex organs

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.920
and impairing fertility
in laboratory animals.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.200
Furthermore,
due to poor regulation

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.160
of dietary supplements,
in the U.S.,

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.440
you never know
what you're gonna be getting.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.480
An analysis
of thirty-one different brands

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.080
of melatonin supplements

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.640
found that the actual
melatonin content varied

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.840
up to nearly 500 percent

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.480
compared to what was listed
on the bottle.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.600
Even within a single brand,

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.120
different lots
of the same product

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.840
suffered similar variability.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.520
Given that there is
no guarantee

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.800
of the strength or purity
of melatonin supplements,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.680
many countries have banned
over-the-counter melatonin,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.240
making it prescription-only

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.520
so authenticity
could be ensured.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.720
U.S. citizens can get
certified melatonin

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.840
by sending a prescription
to an online Canadian pharmacy

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.760
(though it's
technically illegal)

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:56.520
or can get melatonin
from their diet.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.360
Interestingly, the rise
in melatonin blood levels

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.880
or metabolites in the urine

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.320
consistently exceeds
the amount of melatonin

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.160
that's actually ingested
in these foods.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.920
You can even get a spike
in melatonin

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.360
after eating fruit
that doesn't even appear

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.560
to have any detectable
melatonin at all.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.080
The answer to the puzzle
may lie in the gut.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.880
The first site
outside the pineal gland

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.480
where melatonin production
was discovered

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.840
was the human appendix.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.040
Although we now know
melatonin can be produced

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.160
throughout the body,

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.040
the greatest accumulation
appears to be

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.240
in the gastrointestinal tract,

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.880
estimated to contain more than
400 times more melatonin

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.840
than the pineal gland.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.160
So, perhaps the consumption
of certain foods

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.400
can cause the release
of some of this bounty

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.160
into the bloodstream.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.440
This may be
how magnesium supplements

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.360
(500 milligrams a day
for eight weeks)

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.840
was able to improve
sleep quality and quantity

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.920
over placebo, given the effect
was accompanied by a rise

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.800
in melatonin levels.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.960
More intriguing are its
purported anti-aging benefits.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.920
In addition to regulating sleep

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.120
and our circadian rhythms
(when properly timed

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.640
it can be used
to treat jet lag),

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.480
melatonin can have antioxidant

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.880
and anti-inflammatory
properties.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.800
However, secretion of melatonin

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.040
appears to progressively
decline with age,

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.960
dropping as much as 70 percent
between middle and older age.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.560
This has led some to speculate

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.640
that "aging is a syndrome of
relative melatonin deficiency

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.400
resulting from
the gradual failure

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.840
of the pineal gland."

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.880
A variety
of age-related diseases

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.840
such as Alzheimer's
are associated

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.440
with particularly low levels
of melatonin,

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.000
but we have yet to determine

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.360
if this is a cause
or consequence of disease.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.040
Melatonin supplementation
extends the lifespan

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.400
of fruit flies but shortens
the lifespan of C. elegans.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.840
Mice that have had
their pineal glands removed

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.360
appeared to age more rapidly,
but when put to the test,

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.200
melatonin prolonged survival
of some strains of mice,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.520
but shortened the lives
of others (by inducing cancer).

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.480
So, are we more like
New Zealand black mice

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.560
or Bagg albino mice?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.120
Sometimes
the same research group

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.520
went on to publish
opposite results,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.320
showing melatonin
both increasing

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.360
and decreasing lifespan.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.400
Not surprisingly,
a meta-analysis found

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.400
no overall effect

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.120
when all of the mouse studies
were considered together.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.440
In rats, melatonin
significantly improved survival,

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:48.680
but so did
a melatonin-blocking drug.

